# .mcpbignore — extra exclusions on top of mcpb's own built-in list
# (which already strips .git, .DS_Store, *.log, *.map, package-lock.json,
# node_modules/.cache, and similar tooling cruft automatically).
#
# Everything below is repo-level documentation or GitHub-only assets that
# server.js never reads at runtime — safe to leave out of the shipped bundle.

# Repo docs — not used by the running extension
README.md
docs/
.env.example

# GitHub README banner — only images/icon.png is referenced by manifest.json
images/PQHeader.png

# Per-dependency docs bundled inside node_modules — never require()'d at
# runtime, just along for the ride from npm. Safe to drop from the package.
**/*.md
**/*.markdown
**/CHANGELOG*
**/HISTORY*
**/.history/

# sql.js ships every browser/worker/asm.js build variant it has, but
# store.js only ever loads dist/sql-wasm.js (which pulls in sql-wasm.wasm
# alongside it) — the package's own "main" entry confirms this. Everything
# else under dist/ (asm.js fallbacks, worker builds, debug variants,
# browser bundles) is several MB of dead weight for a Node extension.
node_modules/sql.js/dist/*
!node_modules/sql.js/dist/sql-wasm.js
!node_modules/sql.js/dist/sql-wasm.wasm